/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A tiny cluster of solute molecules has two energy terms.
   - γ is the crystal–solution surface energy (J/m²), vm the volume of one molecule in the crystal (m³), k = 1.381 × 10−23 J/K, T in K, S the supersaturation ratio. ΔG rises to a maximum ΔG* at the critical radius r*: smaller clusters tend to re
   - Since ΔG* varies as 1/(ln S)², a modest rise in S lowers the barrier enormously and J jumps by many powers of ten.
   - Growth needs two steps in series.
   - N is the mass deposited per unit area per unit time (kg/m² s), kd the mass-transfer coefficient (m/s), kr the surface rate constant (m/s).
   - McCabe's ΔL law states that geometrically similar crystals of the same substance in the same solution grow by the same length ΔL in the same time, whatever their size: G does not depend on L.
*/
