/* book Worked example 2: Q: Crystals grow by G = kgσ1.5 with kg = 2.5 × 10−6 m/s. (a) Find G at σ = 0.04 in mm/h. (b) How long do 0.10 mm seeds take to reach 0.50 mm? (c) What mass of product does 1 kg of seed give? (d) What σ doubles G?
   1. (a) σ1.5 = 0.041.5 = 0.008. G = 2.5 × 10−6 × 0.008 = 2.0 × 10−8 m/s = 2.0 × 10−8 × 3600 × 1000 = 0.072 mm/h.
   2. (b) ΔL = 0.50 − 0.10 = 0.40 mm; t = 0.40/0.072 = 5.6 h.
   3. (c) By the ΔL law each crystal grows by the same length, so each seed's mass rises by (0.50/0.10)³ = 125. 1 kg of seed gives 125 kg of crystals, so 124 kg of solute must be deposited.
   4. (d) G ∝ σ1.5, so σ must rise by 21/1.5 = 1.587, to 0.0635.
   Answer: G = 0.072 mm/h; 5.6 h to grow from 0.10 to 0.50 mm; 125 kg of product per kg of seed; σ = 0.0635 doubles G. */
